@startuml strategy-pattern
!include style.puml
title Strategy Calculator\n<size:14>Class structure · package calculator</size>
top to bottom direction

class Main <<Client>> {
    {static} + main(args: String[]): void
}

class Calculator <<Context>> {
    - strategy: CalculationStrategy
    + Calculator(strategy: CalculationStrategy)
    + setStrategy(strategy: CalculationStrategy): void
    + calculate(leftOperand: double, rightOperand: double): double
}

interface CalculationStrategy <<interface>> {
    + calculate(leftOperand: double, rightOperand: double): double
}

together {
    class AddStrategy {
        + calculate(double, double): double
    }
    class SubtractStrategy {
        + calculate(double, double): double
    }
    class MultiplyStrategy {
        + calculate(double, double): double
    }
    class DivisionStrategy {
        + calculate(double, double): double
    }
    class PowerStrategy {
        + calculate(double, double): double
    }
}

Main .down.> Calculator : creates / configures
Calculator -down-> "1" CalculationStrategy : strategy / delegates
CalculationStrategy <|.. AddStrategy
CalculationStrategy <|.. SubtractStrategy
CalculationStrategy <|.. MultiplyStrategy
CalculationStrategy <|.. DivisionStrategy
CalculationStrategy <|.. PowerStrategy

' Invisible constraints enforce the order of the concrete strategy row.
AddStrategy -[hidden]right-> SubtractStrategy
SubtractStrategy -[hidden]right-> MultiplyStrategy
MultiplyStrategy -[hidden]right-> DivisionStrategy
DivisionStrategy -[hidden]right-> PowerStrategy

legend bottom
  Solid arrow: navigable association. Each Calculator holds one non-null strategy.
  Dashed line with hollow triangle: interface realization.
  Concrete method parameter names are omitted for compactness; types are exact.
  Calculator is final. Main also creates all concrete strategies; see client-wiring.
endlegend
@enduml
